hadiths[144]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7345","“When Allah assembles the first and the last on the Day of Resurrection, a day concerning which there is no doubt, a caller will cry out: ‘Whoever used to associate anyone else in an action that he did for Allah, let him seek his reward from someone other than Allah, for Allah is so self-sufficient that He has no need of any associate.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4203)"
"7346","I saw them, I liked them. I asked: O my Lord! Who are these? Allah Almighty said: Your brother Musa bin Imran and his followers from Bani Israel. I asked: O my Lord! Where is my nation? The Lord said: Look to your right. I looked, and there was a mountain of Makkah blackened with the faces of people. I asked: O my Lord! Who are these people? The Lord said: This is your nation, are you pleased? I said: O my Lord! I am pleased. The Lord said: Look to your left. I looked in that direction, and the horizon was filled with the faces of people. I asked: O my Lord! Who are these people? The Lord said: This is your nation, are you pleased? I said: O my Lord! I am pleased. Then it was said: Along with these people, there are seventy thousand such people who will enter Paradise without any reckoning. The narrator states: Sayyiduna ‘Ukasha bin Mihsan (may Allah be pleased with him), who belonged to Banu Asad bin Khuzaymah, stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah! Pray to Allah Almighty that He includes me among them. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You are among them. Another person said: O Messenger of Allah! Pray to Allah Almighty that He includes me among them. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ‘Ukasha has preceded you in this matter."
"7347","While Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up to deliver a sermon, he said: 0 people, Allah would make you assemble barefooted, naked and uncircumcised (and then recited the words of the Qur'an):"" As We created you for the first time, We shall repeat it. (It is) a promise (binding) upon us. Lo! We are to perform it, and the first person who would be clothed on the Day of Resurrection would be (Hadrat) Ibrahim (peace be upon him)"" and, behold! some persons of my Ummah would be brought and taken to the left and I would say: My Lord, they are my companions, and it would be said: You do not know what they did after you, and I would say just as the pious servant (Hadrat 'Isa) said:, I was a witness regarding them as I remained among them and Thou art a witness over everything, so if Thou chastisest them, they are Thy servants and if Thou for- givest them, Thou art Mighty, Wise"" (v. 117-118). And it would be said to him: They constantly turned to their heels since you left them. This hadith has been transmitted on the authority of Waki' and Mu'adh (and the words are):"" What new things they fabricated."" (Using translation from Muslim 2860b)"
"7348",""" O Messenger of Allah! When will the Hour be established?"" So the Propher ﷺ stood to perform Salat and when he was finished his Salat he said: ""Where is the one who asked when the hour will be established?"" The man said: ""It was I, O Mesenger of Allah!"" He said: ""What have you prepared for it?"" He said: ""O Messenger of allah! I have not prepared very much of salat nor fasting for it, but I love Allah and His Messenger."" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""A man shall be with whom ever he loves, and you shall be with whomever you love."" So after the advent of Islam, I did not see that anything brought the Muslims more happiness than that. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2385)"
"7349","that regarding the saying of Allah, Most High: ""The Day when We shall call together all human beings with their (respective) Imam (17:71)"" the Prophet ﷺ said: ""One of you will be called out to be given his record in his right hand, he will be grown in his body to sixty forearm-lengths, his face will be whitened, and a crown of sparkling pearls will be placed upon his head. So he will go to his companions, who can see him from afar, and they will say: 'O Allah! Bring this one to us, and let us be blessed by him.' Until he reaches them, and says to them: 'Receive the good news! For each man among you shall be the likes of this.'"" [He ﷺ said:] ""As for the disbeliever, then his face shall be blackened, he will be grown in his body to sixty forearm-lengths in the image of Adam, he will given a crown, and his companions will see him and say: 'We seek refuge in Allah from the evil of this one. O Allah! Do not bring this one to us.'"" He said: ""So when he reaches them, they say: 'O Allah! Take him away' so they will be told: 'May Allah cast you away! Indeed for each man among you is the likes of this.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3136)"
"7350","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person from among the people of Hell will be brought, and the Lord will say to him: O son of Adam, how did you find your abode? He will say: O Lord, it is the worst abode. The Lord will say: Are you willing to give as ransom the equivalent of all the gold on the face of the earth? He will say: Yes, my Lord. Then the Lord will say: You are lying. You were asked for something much easier than this (but you did not act upon it). Then he will be take"
"7351","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: On the Day of Resurrection, it will be said to the disbeliever: What do you think"
"7352","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""On the Day of Resurrection, for the disbeliever, the day will be as long as fifty thousand years, and the disbelieving person will see Hell and will think that he will keep falling into it for forty years."
"7353","What is this hadith that you narrate that the Last Hour would come at such and such time? Thereupon he said: Hallowed be Allah, there is no god but Allah (or the words to the same effect). I have decided that I would not narrate anything to anyone now. I had only said that you would see after some time an important event that the (sacred) House (Ka'ba) would be burnt and it would happen and definitely happen. He then reported that Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The Dajjal would appear in my Ummah and he would stay (in the world) for forty - I cannot say whether he meant forty days, forty months or forty years. And Allah would then send Jesus son of Mary who would resemble 'Urwa b Mas'ud. He (Jesus Christ) would chase him and kill him. Then people would live for seven years that there would be no rancour between two persons. Then Allah would send cold wind from the side of Syria that none would survive upon the earth having a speck of good in him or faith in him but he would die, so much so that even if some amongst you were to enter the innermost part of the mountain, this wind would reach that place also and that would cause his death. I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Only the wicked people would survive and they would be as careless as birds with the characteristics of beasts. They would never appreciate the good nor condemn evil. Then Satan would come to them in human form and would say: Don't you respond? And they would say: What do you order us? And he would command them to worship the idols but, in spite of this, they would have abundance of sustenance and lead comfortable lives. Then the trumpet would be blown and no one would hear that but he would bend his neck to one side and raise it from the other side and the first one to hear that trumpet would be the person who would be busy in setting right the tank meant for providing water to the camels. He would swoon and the other people would also swoon, then Allah would send or He would cause to send rain which would be like dew and there would grow out of it the bodies of the people. Then the second trumpet would be blown and they would stand up and begin to look (around). Then it would be said: O people, go to your Lord, and make them stand there. And they would be questioned. Then it would be said: Bring out a group (out of them) for the Hell-Fire. And then it would be asked: How much? It would be said: Nine hundred and ninty-nine out of one thousand for the Hell-Fire and that would be the day which would make the children old because of its terror and that would be the day about which it has been said: ""On the day when the shank would be uncovered"" (lxviii. 42). (Using translation from Muslim 2940a)"
"7354","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: This verse was revealed: \""O people! Fear your Lord. Indeed, the earthquake of the Hour is a tremendous thing.\"" This verse was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) while he was traveling. He recited it in a loud voice until his companions gathered near him. He said: Do you know what day this is? (Meaning, what day is the Day of Resurrection?) On that day, Allah Almighty will say to Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him):"
"7355","""We were with 'Abdullah bin 'Umar when he was circumambulating the House; a man came up to him and said: 'O Ibn 'Umar, what did you hear the Messenger of Allah say about the Najwa?' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'On the Day of Resurrection, the believer will be brought close to his Lord until He will cover him with His screen, then He will make him confess his sins. He will ask him: ""Do you confess?"" He will say: ""O Lord, I confess."" This will continue as long as Allah wills, then He will say: ""I concealed them for you in the world, and I forgive you for them today."" Then he will be given the scroll of his good deeds, or his record, in his right hand. But as for the disbeliever or the hypocrite, (his sins) will be announced before the witnesses.' "" (One of the narrators) Khalid said: ""At: 'before the witnesses' there is something missing."" ""These are the ones who lied against their Lord!' No doubt! The curse of Allah is on the wrongdoers."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 183)"
"7356","The curse of Allah is upon the wrongdoers.'"
"7357","The foolish person will say: O my Lord! Islam came and at that time children would pelt me with dung (meaning my mental state was not sound). As for the insane person, he will say: When Islam came, I had no understanding of anything. As for the person who died during the period of interval, he will say: O my Lord! No messenger of Yours came to me. Then the Lord will take a covenant from these people that they will certainly obey Him. Then the Lord will send a messenger to them (saying): Enter the Hellfire. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) says: By the One in Whose hand is my soul, if they enter it, it will be cool and safe for them."
"7358","We were in the company of Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he smiled, and said: Do you know why I laughed? We said: Allah and His Messenger, know best. Thereupon he said: It was because (there came to my mind the) talk which the servant would have with his Lord (on the Day of judgment). He would say: My Lord, have you not guaranteed me protection against injustice? He would say: Yes. Then the servant would say: I do not deem valid any witness against me but my own self, and He would say: Well, enough would be the witness of your self against you and that of the two angels who had been appointed to record your deeds. Then the seal would be set upon his mouth and it would be said to his hands and feet to speak and they would speak of his deeds. Then the mouth would be made free to talk, he would say (to the hands and feet): Be away, let there be curse of Allah upon you. It was for your safety that I contended. (Using translation from Muslim 2969)"
"7359","Do you know who is poor? They (the Companions of the Holy Prophet) said: A poor man amongst us is one who has neither dirham with him nor wealth. He (the Holy Prophet) said: The poor of my Umma would be he who would come on the Day of Resurrection with prayers and fasts and Zakat but (he would find himself bankrupt on that day as he would have exhausted his funds of virtues) since he hurled abuses upon others, brought calumny against others and unlawfully consumed the wealth of others and shed the blood of others and beat others, and his virtues would be credited to the account of one (who suffered at his hand). And if his good deeds fall short to clear the account, then his sins would be entered in (his account) and he would be thrown in the Hell-Fire. (Using translation from Muslim 2581)"
"7360","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: That Day it will declare its information. And said: 'Do you know what its information is?' they said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'Indeed its information is that it will testify against every servant, male and female, It will say that he did such and such, on such and such a day.' He said: 'With this it shall be ordered.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2429)"
"7361","narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever has wronged his brother with regard to his honor or wealth, let him seek his forgiveness today, before a day comes when there will be no dinar or dirham. If he has good deeds, they will be taken from him in proportion to his wrongdoing, and if he does not have good deeds, then the sins of his companion will be taken and placed upon him."
"7362","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on the servant who has wronged his brother regarding his life or wealth, then comes to his brother and seeks forgiveness for his wrongdoing before his good deeds are taken, and if he has no good deeds, then his companion's sins are taken and added to his sins."
"7363","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “(On the Day of Resurrection) rights will surely be given to their rightful owners, to the extent that the hornless goat will be given retribution from the horned goat, which had butted it with its horns.”"
"7364","I not make your body healthy? Did I not quench your thirst with cool water?"
"7365","I not make hearing and sight for you? Did I not grant you wealth and children? Then what deeds did you do? That person will look in front of him, behind him, to his right, and to his left, but he will find nothing. He will only be able to save himself from Hell with his face. So you people should try to save yourselves from Hell, even if it is with half a date, and if you do not find even that, then try to save yourselves from Hell with a pure word."
"7366","Verily, Allah, the Exalted and Glorious, would say on the Day of Resurrection: O son of Adam, I was sick but you did not visit Me. He would say: O my Lord; how could I visit Thee whereas Thou art the Lord of the worlds? Thereupon He would say: Didn't you know that such and such servant of Mine was sick but you did not visit him and were you not aware of this that if you had visited him, you would have found Me by him? O son of Adam, I asked food from you but you did not feed Me. He would say: My Lord, how could I feed Thee whereas Thou art the Lord of the worlds? He said: Didn't you know that such and such servant of Mine asked food from you but you did not feed him, and were you not aware that if you had fed him you would have found him by My side? (The Lord would again say: ) O son of Adam, I asked drink from you but you did not provide Me. He would say: My Lord, how could I provide Thee whereas Thou art the Lord of the worlds? Thereupon He would say: Such and such of servant of Mine asked you for a drink but you did not provide him, and had you provided him drink you would have found him near Me. (Using translation from Muslim 2569)"
"7367","I not subjugate horses and camels for you? Did I not make you affluent? Did I not marry you to such-and-such woman, to whom many people had sent marriage proposals, but I did not let them marry her and arranged your marriage with her?"
"7368","I believed in You and separated myself from the people (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) I separated myself from the people and I believed in You."
"7369","I said: O Messenger of Allah! (Allah the Exalted says:) ""Whoever is given his record in his right hand, he will be given an easy reckoning."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This refers to presentation only; otherwise, whoever is taken to account on the Day of Resurrection will be doomed."
"7370","""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'Whoever his account is questioned about , he shall be ruined.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Indeed Allah [Most High] has said: Then as for him who shall be given his Record in his right hand. He surely will receive an easy reckoning.' Then he said: 'That is the presentation.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2426)"
"7371","The command of Allah, the Exalted, is:) 'The person whose book of deeds will be given in his right hand, an easy reckoning will be taken from him.'"" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This refers to being presented (with the deeds). Otherwise, on the Day of Resurrection, whoever is actually taken to account will be ruined."
"7372","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(It means) that the Lord looks at a person's book of deeds and then forgives his sins, because on that day, whoever is strictly taken to account will be doomed."" Whatever calamity befalls a believer, it erases his sins, even if it is a thorn that pricks him (that too erases his sins)."
"7373","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'There is no one among you but his Lord will speak to him without any intermediary between them. He will look to his right and will not see anything but that which he sent forth. He will look to his left and will not see anything but that which he sent forth. Then he will look in front of him and will be faced with the Fire. So whoever among you can protect himself from fire, even by means of half a date, let him do so.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 185)"
"7374","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: As for banditry, soon there will come a time upon you when a caravan will depart from Hira and reach Makkah and it will have nothing to fear. As for poverty, the Hour will not be established until a person will go out with his zakat and will not find anyone to accept it from him. Each one of you will be made to stand before Allah; there will be no veil between him and Allah to prevent him, nor any interpreter between them. Then the Lord will say to him: Did I not give you wealth? He will reply: Yes. The Lord will say: Did I not send a messenger to you? He will reply: Yes. Then the person will look to his right and will see nothing but Hellfire, and he will look to his left and will see nothing but Hellfire. So each one of you should try to save himself from the Fire, even if it be with half a date, and if he does not find that, then with a good word (he should try to save himself from the Fire)."
"7375",""" I know the last of the people of the Fire to depart from the Fire and the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise. A man will be brought forth and He ﷺ will say: 'Ask about his small sins and hide his large sins.' So it will be said to him: 'Did you do this and that on such and such a day, did you do this and that on such- and – such a day?'” He said: “Then it will be said to him; 'For each of your sins you shall have a reward.'” He ﷺ said: “So he will say: 'O Lord! I have done things that I do not see here.'” He (Abu Dharr) said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laugh until his molars were visible.” (Sahih) (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2596)"
"7376",""" I was with a troop in Jerusalem, and a man among them said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: ""From the intersection of one man in my Ummah more (people) then Banu Tamim will be admitted into Paradise.' It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Someone other than you?' He said: 'Other than me.' So when he stood, I said: 'Who is this?' They said: 'This is Ibn Abi Al-Jadh'a.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2438)"
"7377","I am your Lord. Only the Prophets will speak with Him. Then it will be said: Is there any sign between you and Him by which you will recognize Him? The Muslims will say: The Shin. Then the veil will be lifted from the Shin, and every believer will fall in prostration before Him, and the one who used to prostrate for show and hypocrisy will remain. He will try to prostrate, but his back will become stiff. Then a bridge will be brought and placed over Hell. We asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is the bridge? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: It is a slippery place where one may fall. On it are hooks, thorns, and sharp things, like the thorns of a particular plant in Najd called Sa‘dan. Some believers will cross it in the blink of an eye, some like lightning, some like the wind, some like fast horses, and some like mounted men. Some will cross it safely, some will be scratched, and some will be affected by the flames of Hell, until the last of them will crawl across it. The truth will become clear to the believers at that time when they see that they have been saved, and some of their brothers remain, who will say: O our Lord, these are our brothers; they used to pray with us, fast with us, and do deeds with us. So the Lord will say: Go and take out from the Fire anyone in whose heart you find faith equal to the weight of a dinar. Allah will make their faces forbidden for the Fire. They will come to their brothers, some of whom will be engulfed up to their feet, some up to half their shins. Then they will come out of Hell. Then they will return again. Then He will say: Go and take out from the Fire anyone in whose heart you find faith equal to half a dinar. So they will take them out. Then they will come a third time, and it will be said: Go and take out from the Fire anyone in whose heart you find faith equal to the weight of a grain. So they will take them out. Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) says: If you do not believe my words, then recite this verse: Allah, the Exalted, has said: “Indeed, Allah does not wrong even the weight of a speck. If there is a good deed, He multiplies it and grants from Himself a great reward.” Angels, Prophets, and the truthful will intercede. Then the Mighty, Blessed, and Exalted One, besides Whom there is no deity, will say: Now My intercession remains. Then the Compeller (Allah) will take out a handful of people from Hell, those who had been burnt to coal, and they will be thrown into a river called the River of Life. They will sprout forth in it as a seed sprouts forth in the silt carried by a flood. Have you not seen it at the edge of a rock or the base of a tree? The part facing the sun is green, and the part in the shade is white. So they will come out shining like pearls. Rings will be placed around their necks. They will enter Paradise, and the people of Paradise will say: These are the ones whom the Most Merciful has freed (from Hell). Allah will admit them into Paradise without any deed they did or any good they sent forth. It will be said to them: Whatever you see is yours, and the like of it as well. Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) says: It has reached me that the Bridge (Sirat) will be thinner than a hair and sharper than a sword. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The word “Shin” refers to severity (i.e., the matter will become severe)."
"7378","I am listening.' Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) will submit, 'O my Lord, You have burned my children.' So the Lord will say, 'Take out from Hell every person in whose heart there is (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) as much faith as the weight of a barley grain.'"
"7379","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""People will pass over the bridge of Hell. Upon it will be large hooks and spikes, which will snatch people from the right and from the left. On both sides of it, there will be angels present, and they will be saying: O Allah, grant safety, grant safety. Some people will pass as swiftly as the wind, some like a fast horse, some like a running person, some like a walk"
"7380",": : "" "" . Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is your opinion about this statement of Allah: 'On the Day when the earth will be changed to another earth, and the heavens (as well), and all people will appear before Allah, the One, the Irresistible.' So where will the people be at that time?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""They will be on the Bridge of Sirat."
"7381","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day to his Companions: ‘Who will strive hard with sincerity for Paradise? For there is nothing like Paradise. By the Lord of the Ka’bah, it is sparkling light, sweet basil waving in the breeze, a lofty palace, a flowing river, abundant ripe fruit, a beautiful wife and many fine garments, in a palace of eternal abode, in ease and luxury, in beautiful, strongly-built, lofty houses.’ They said: ‘We will strive heard for it, O Messenger of Allah.’ He said: ‘Say: In sha’ Allah (if Allah wills).’ Then he mentioned Jihad and encouraged them to engage in it.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4332)"
"7382","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever unjustly kills a dhimmi (non-Muslim under Muslim protection) will not even smell the fragrance of Paradise, although its fragrance can be perceived from a distance of one hundred miles."
"7383","“Whoever claims to belong to someone other than his father will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, even though its fragrance may be detected from a distance of five hundred years.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2611)"
"7384","The narrator says) To my knowledge, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""You will recognize the people of Paradise in comparison to the people of Hell."" One of the Muslims asked: O Messenger of Allah! By what means? The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Through good praise and bad praise, you are witnesses over one another."
"7385","The same hadith has been by AlMughirah bin Shu’bah attributing it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. (Using translation from Muslim 189a)"
"7386","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Two gardens, the utensils and the contents of which are of silver, and two other gardens, the utensils and contents of which are of gold. And nothing will prevent the people who will be in the Garden of Eden from seeing their Lord except the curtain of Majesty over His Face."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 4878)"
"7387","""We said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What is wrong with us that when we are with you our hearts are softened and we feel free of desire for this world, and we are of the people of the Hereafter. But when we depart from you and socialize with our families and our children, we do not recognize ourselves(i.e., we are changed persons)?' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If you were to be in that condition when you depart from me, the angels would have surely visited you in your houses. And if you did not sin, Allah would surely have brought anew creation that they may sin, so that then He may forgive them.'""He said: ""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! From what was the creation created?' He said: 'From water.' We said: 'Paradise, what is it constructed of?' He said,'Bricks of silver and bricks of gold. Its mortar is musk of a strong fragrance, and its pebbles are pearls and rubies, and its earth is saffron. Whoever enters it shall live and shall not suffer, and shall feel joy and shall not die, nor shall their clothes wear out, nor shall their youth come to an end.' Then he said: 'Three persons , their supplication is not rejected: The just ruler, the fasting person when he breaks his fast, and the supplication of the wronged person. It is raised up above the clouds, and the gates of Heaven are opened up for it, and the Lord, Blessed and Exalted says: I shall surely come to your aid, even if after a time.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2526)"
"7388","The distance between the two gates of Paradise is the span of seven years' journey."
"7389","The narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) as much as the distance between Makkah and Busra."
"7390","The distance between two of these levels is as great as that between the heavens and the earth. When you ask (from Allah), then ask for Jannat al-Firdaws, for it is the middle and highest part of Paradise, and above it is the Throne, and from it the rivers of Paradise flow."
"7391","Um (the mother of) Haritha came to Messenger of Allah ﷺ after Haritha had been martyred on the Day (of the battle) of Badr by an arrow thrown by an unknown person. She said, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! You know the position of Haritha in my heart (i.e. how dear to me he was), so if he is in Paradise, I will not weep for him, or otherwise, you will see what I will do."" The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Are you mad? Is there only one Paradise? There are many Paradises, and he is in the highest Paradise of Firdaus."" The Prophet added, ""A forenoon journey or an after noon journey in Allah's Cause is better than the whole world and whatever is in it; and a place equal to an arrow bow of anyone of you, or a place equal to a foot in Paradise is better than the whole world and whatever is in it; and if one of the women of Paradise looked at the earth, she would fill the whole space between them (the earth and the heaven) with light, and would fill whatever is in between them, with perfume, and the veil of her face is better than the whole world and whatever is in it."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6567)"
"7392","The people of Paradise will see each other in the lofty chambers of Paradise just as you see a shining star setting on the eastern or western horizon.”"
"7393","The inmates of Paradise would see the inmates of the apartment over them just as you see the shining planets which remain in the eastern and the western horizon because of the superiority some have over others. They said: Messenger of Allah, would in these abodes of Apostles others besides them not be able to reach? He said: Yes, they will, by Him, in Whose hand is my life, those who believe in God and acknowledge the Truth, will reach them. (Using translation from Muslim 2831b)"
"7394","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When Allah created Paradise, He said to Gabriel: Go and look at it. He went and looked at it, then came and said: O my Lord! By Thy might, no one who hears of it will fail to enter it. He then surrounded it with disagreeable things, and said: Go and look at it, Gabriel. He went and looked at it, then came and said: O my Lord! By Thy might, I am afraid that no one will enter it. When Allah created Hell, He said: Go and look at it, Gabriel. He went and looked at it, then came and said: O my Lord! By Thy might, no one who hears of it will enter it. He then surrounded it with desirable things and said: Go and look at it, Gabriel. He went, looked at it, then came and said: O my Lord! By Thy might and power, I am afraid that no one will remain who does not enter it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4744)"
"7395","Abu Bakr b. Abdullah b. Qais reported on the authority of his father that Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that in Paradise there would be a tent made of a single hollowed pearl, the breadth of which would be sixty miles from all sides and there would live a family in each corner and the other would not be able to see the believer who goes around them. (Using translation from Muslim 2838b)"
"7396","The whiteness of the shin of a woman from among the people of Paradise will be visible from beneath seventy silk garments. The reason for this is that Allah Almighty has said: 'They are like rubies and coral.' Ruby is such a stone that if you put a thread through it and then look at it, you will be able to see it through the stone."
"7397","I am from the additional blessings.' That woman will be wearing seventy types of garments, and when the inhabitant of Paradise looks at her, he will see the marrow of her shin from behind those garments. And those women will be wearing crowns, and the least of the pearls on them (will be so bright) that it will illuminate the space between the east and the west."
"7398","That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""To go out in the cause of Allah in the morning, or the afternoon, is better than the world and what is in it. And the space that a bow of one of you - or the space that his hand - would occupy in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it. And if a woman among the women inhabiting Paradise were to appear to the people of the earth, then she would illuminate what is between the ( the heavens and the earth), and a pleasant scent would fill up what is between them, and the scarf on her head is better than the world and what is in it."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1651)"
"7399","The scarf on her head is better than the world and everything in it."
"7400","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A man will be given such and such wives in Paradise. It was asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Who will have the strength for so many?"" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A man will be given the strength of one hundred men."
"7401","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Even the lowest-ranking inhabitant of Paradise will have 80,000 servants and 72 wives. For him there will be a tent made of pearls, emeralds, and rubies, so large that its size will be equal to the distance from Jabiyah to Sana'a."
"7402","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: It was asked in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), ""Will we have intercourse in Paradise?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""Yes, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul. You will have intercourse in the best manner, and when the man gets up from the woman, she will become pure and virgin again."""
"7406","The roof of my house was opened and Sayyiduna Jibril (peace be upon him) descended. He opened my chest and washed it with the water of Zamzam. Then he brought a basin filled with wisdom and faith. He poured it into my chest and then closed it up. Then he took my hand and ascended with me towards the sky. When we reached the lowest heaven, Sayyiduna Jibril (peace be upon him) said to the guardian of the lowest heaven: Open the door. He asked: Who is it? He replied: Jibril. He asked: Is there anyone with you? He replied: With me is Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). He asked: Has he been sent for? He replied: Yes! So the door was opened. When we ascended to the lowest heaven, there was a man there, on his right were many people and on his left were many people. When he looked to his right, he would laugh, and when he looked to his left, he would weep. He said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous son. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I asked: O Jibril, who is this? He replied: This is Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him), and those on his right and left are his offspring. Those on his right are the people of Paradise, and those on his left are the people of Hell. When he looks to his right, he laughs, and when he looks to his left, he weeps. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then Jibril took me to the second heaven. He said to its guardian: Open the door. Its guardian asked him the same as the guardian of the lowest heaven had asked. Then he opened the door. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) met Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him), Sayyiduna Idris (peace be upon him), Sayyiduna Isa (peace be upon him), Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him), and Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) in the heavens. May Allah's blessings be upon Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and upon them. However, the narrator did not clarify the specific locations of these individuals. He only mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) found Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him) in the lowest heaven and Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) in the sixth heaven. Ibn Shihab Zuhri says: Ibn Hazm informed me that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) and Sayyiduna Abu Habba Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then he ascended with me until I reached the Station of Istawa, where I heard the sound of the pens moving."" Ibn Hazm says: Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: There, Allah made fifty prayers obligatory upon my Ummah. I returned and passed by Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him). Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) asked: What has your Lord enjoined upon your Ummah? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I replied: He has enjoined fifty prayers upon them. Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) said: Return to your Lord, for your Ummah will not be able to bear that. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I returned to my Lord and He reduced them by half. I returned to Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) and informed him. He said: Return to your Lord, for your Ummah will not be able to bear that. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I turned to my Lord and He said: These will be five prayers, but they will be counted as fifty. Our word does not change. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I returned to Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) and informed him. He said: Return to your Lord. I said: I feel shy before my Lord. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then he (i.e., Jibril) proceeded with me until he brought me to Sidrat al-Muntaha, which was covered with various colors. I do not know what they were. Then I was admitted into Paradise, where there were buildings made of pearls and its soil was like musk."
"7407","The pebbles of the people of Paradise will be of gold and their incense burners will burn aloe wood."
"7408","The rivers of Paradise flow from beneath a mound (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) from beneath mountains, which are made of musk."
"7409","""Indeed in Paradise there is a sea of water, and a sea of honey,and a sea of milk, and a sea of wine, then the rivers shall split off afterwards."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2571)"
"7410","""There is not a tree in Paradise except that its tree is of gold."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2525)"
"7411","“In Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider could travel for one hundred years and never leave it.” ""Recite, if you wish: 'And in shade long-extended (56:30).'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4335)"
"7412","“In Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider could travel for one hundred years and never leave it.” ""Recite, if you wish: 'And in shade long-extended (56:30).'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4335)"
"7413","The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""It is a tree in Paradise whose span is one hundred years. The clothes of the people of Paradise will come out from its branches."
"7414","The Prophet said, ""In Paradise, there is a tree called Tuba."" The Bedouin asked, ""Which of our trees resembles it?"" The Prophet said, ""None of the trees in your region resemble it. Have you been to Syria?"" He replied, ""No, O Messenger of Allah!"" The Prophet said, ""In Syria, there is a tree called Jamizah. Its trunk is tied and then the upper part is opened."" The Bedouin asked, ""How large is the root of (that tree in Paradise)?"" The Prophet said, ""If you were to saddle a young camel from among your household's camels and set it off, you would not be able to cross its root until the camel's bones break due to old age."
"7415","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed those people of this matter. He said: The Sidrat al-Muntaha was brought before"
"7416","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes. He asked: How big will its clusters be? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: As far as the distance that a ""spotted crow"" covers in a month of continuous flight without stopping. The Bedouin asked: How big will its single grape be? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: Has your father ever slaughtered a large male goat from among his goats? He replied: Yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: Did he also skin it and give the skin to your mother and say: Take this, tan it for us and then make a water bag from it so that we may water our animals with it? The Bedouin replied: Yes. Then he said: A single grape will suffice me and all my family. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes, and it will suffice most of your family as well."
"7417","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Indeed the space in Paradise taken up by a whip, is better than the world and what is in it. Recite if you wish: 'And whoever is moved away from the Fire and admitted to Paradise, he indeed is successful. The life of this world is only the enjoyment of deception (3:185).'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3013)"
"7418","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A place in Paradise as much as the space occupied by a bow, or the place where a whip is kept, is better than the world."
"7419","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) says, ""Then those people will stand up, and it will be said to them: What deeds did you do?"" They will say, ""O our Lord, You put us to trial, so we acted with patience. You gave wealth and authority to others."" Then Allah Almighty will say, ""You have spoken the truth."" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) says, ""Then those people will enter Paradise before the others, and the severity of reckoning will remain for the wealthy and the rulers."" The people asked, ""Where will the believers be on that day?"" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Chairs of light will be placed for them and clouds will shade them, and that day will be shorter for the people of faith than even an hour of a (worldly) day."
"7420","narrator Sufyan is in doubt.) Each of them will have two wives, the marrow of whose shins will be visible from beneath the flesh, and there will be no unmarried person in Paradise."
"7421","The people replied, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among Allah's creation, the first to enter Paradise will be the poor emigrants, for whom the paths were closed and calamities were created for them. When one of them would die, his need would remain in his chest and he would not have the ability to fulfill it. Then Allah, from among the angels, will say to whomever He wills: Bring them and greet them with peace. The angels will say, 'O our Lord! We are the inhabitants of Your heavens and the best among Your creation. Are You commanding us to go to them and greet them with peace?' The Lord will say: These are the servants who worshipped Me and did not associate anyone with Me. The paths were closed for them and calamities were created for them. When one of them died, his need remained in his chest and he did not have the ability to fulfill it."" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) says: ""At that time, the angels will come to those people and will enter upon them from every door (and will say what is mentioned in the Qur'an): 'Peace be upon you for what you patiently endured. And excellent is the final home.'"
"7422","While I was standing beside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one of the rabbis of the Jews came and said: Peace be upon you, O Muhammad. I pushed him backwith a push that he was going to fall. Upon this he said: Why do you push me? I said: Why don't you say: O Messenger of Allah? The Jew said: We call him by the name by which he was named by his family. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: My name is Muhammad with which I was named by my family. The Jew said: I have come to ask you (something). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Should that thing be of any benefit to you, if I tell you that? He (the Jew) said: I will lend my ears to it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew a line with the help of the stick that he had with him and then said: Ask (whatever you like). Thereupon the Jew said: Where would the human beings be on the Daywhen the earth would change into another earth and the heavens too (would change into other heavens)? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: They would be in darkness beside the Bridge. He (the Jew) again said: Who amongst people would be the first to cross (this bridge).? He said: They would be the poor amongst the refugees. The Jew said: What would constitute their breakfast when they would enter Paradise? He (the Holy Prophet) replied: A caul of the fish-liver. He (the Jew) said. What would be their food alter this? He (the Holy Prophet) said: A bullockwhich was fed in the different quarters of Paradise would be slaughtered for them. He (the Jew) said: What would be their drink? He (the Holy Prophet) said: They would be given drink from the fountain which is named"" Salsabil"". He (the Jew) said: I have come to ask you about a thing which no one amongst the people on the earth knows except an apostle or one or two men besides him. He (the Holy Prophet) said: Would it benefit you if I tell you that? He (the Jew) said: I would lend ears to that. He then said: I have come to ask you about the child. He (the Holy Prophet) said: The reproductive substance of man is white and that of woman (i. e. ovum central portion) yellow, and when they have sexual intercourse and the male's substance (chromosomes and genes) prevails upon the female's substance (chromosomes and genes), it is the male child that is created by Allah's Decree, and when the substance of the female prevails upon the substance contributed by the male, a female child is formed by the Decree of Allah. The Jew said: What you have said is true; verily you are an Apostle. He then returned and went away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He asked me about such and such things of which I have had no knowledge till Allah gave me that. (Using translation from Muslim 315a)"
"7423","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Just now Jibreel has informed me about them. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Salam (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He (Jibreel) is disliked by the Jews. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: As for resemblance, when the man’s fluid prevails over the woman’s fluid, the child resembles the father, and if the woman’s fluid prevails over the man’s fluid, the child resembles the mother. The first thing that will gather people together is a fire that will come from the east and will gather them and drive them towards the west. The first thing the people of Paradise will eat will be the caudate lobe of the liver of a fish and the head of a bull. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah! The Jews are slanderous people. If they hear that I have believed in you, they will slander me and speak against me, so I wish to call them. Then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Salam (may Allah be pleased with him) sent for them and the Jews came. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: What is the status of Abdullah bin Salam among you? They said: He is our chief and the son of our chief, our scholar and the son of our scholar, our best man and the son of our best man. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If he becomes Muslim, will you also become Muslim? They said: May Allah protect him from saying such a thing; he could never do that. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Ibn Salam, come out. He came out before them and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah. The Jews said: Rather, he is our worst man and the son of our worst man, our most ignorant man and the son of our most ignorant man. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Salam (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! Did I not tell you that they are slanderous people?"
"7424","Sayyiduna Zaid bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A Jew came to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: O Abul Qasim! Do you believe that the people of Paradise will eat and drink in Paradise? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: By Him in Whose hand is my soul, every person of Paradise will be given the strength of a hundred men in eating, drinking, desire, and intercourse. The Jews said to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and b"
"7425","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: In Paradise, there is a market in which the people of Paradise will come every Friday. There are mounds of musk in it, and a wind will blow from the north, sprinkling musk on their faces. When they return to their wives, they will say, ""After us, Allah has increased your beauty and elegance."" Their families will say to them, ""After us, Allah has also increased your beauty and elegance."
"7426","""While he was on the Minbar, I heard Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah saying - and he attributed it to the Prophet ﷺ - 'Indeed Musa [peace be upon him] asked his Lord: ""O Lord! Who is the lowest in rank among the people of Paradise?"" He said: ""A man who comes after the people of Paradise have been admitted to Paradise, and he is told to enter. He says: 'How can I enter when they have gotten all of their abodes, and all that is to be had?'"" He said: ""So it is said to him: 'Would you accept if you were to have what a king in the world?' He says: 'Yes, O Lord! I accept.' So it is said to him: 'Then for you is this and its like, and its like again, and its like again.' So he says: 'I accept, O Lord!' So it is said to him: 'Then for you is this and ten the like thereof.' So he says: 'I accept, O Lord!' So it is said: 'Indeed you shall have this, and whatever your soul desires, and whatever delights your eyes.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3198)"
"7427","The people of the world used to wish for things in their world and used to suffer from scarcity regarding the world. I ask You for something like that. The Lord will say: You will get something like that and ten times more (in addition). (The Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, says: Allah Almighty said:) This is the rank of the lowest person in Paradise."
"7428","I think these words are also in the narration: He could arrange their marriages. Yet, the blessings he possesses would not decrease in the least."
"7429","I am your Lord.' They will say, 'We seek refuge with Allah from you; we will stay here until our Lord comes to us. When our Lord comes to us, we will recognize Him.' The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Their Lord will come to them in the form they know, and He will say, 'I am your Lord.' They will say, 'You are our Lord.' Then a bridge will be laid over Hell. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I will be the first to cross it. On that day, all the Messengers will be saying, 'O Allah, grant safety! O Allah, grant safety!' And there will be hooks on that bridge like the thorns of the Sa'dan plant. Do you know what the thorns of Sa'dan are like?"" The people replied, ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah!"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""They will be like the thorns of Sa'dan, but only Allah knows their size, and they will snatch people according to their deeds. Some will be destroyed because of their deeds, and some will fall into Hell and then be saved, until Allah Almighty finishes judging between His servants and intends to bring out from Hell those who used to testify that there is no god but Allah. Allah Almighty will command the angels to bring them out, and the angels will recognize them by the marks of prostration."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah Almighty has forbidden Hell to consume the marks of prostration on the son of Adam. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: They will bring them out while they have been burnt and turned into charcoal. Water will be poured over them, which is called the Water of Life, and they will grow like a seed grows in the silt left by a flood. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: One man among them will remain, who will come crawling on his face in Hell and will say, ""O my Lord! Its stench has distressed me and its heat has burnt me. Turn my face away from Hell."" He will keep supplicating, so Allah Almighty will say, ""If I grant you this, will you ask for anything else?"" He will say, ""By Your honor, I will not ask for anything else."" Allah Almighty will turn his face away from Hell. Then the man will say, ""O my Lord! Bring me near the gate of Paradise."" Allah Almighty will say, ""Did you not say that you would not ask Me for anything else? O son of Adam, how treacherous you are!"" Then the man will keep supplicating, and the Lord will say, ""If I grant you this, will you ask for anything else?"" He will say, ""By Your honor, I will not ask for anything else."" Then he will make a firm promise to Allah Almighty that he will not ask for anything else, so Allah Almighty will bring him near the gate of Paradise. When Allah Almighty brings him near the gate of Paradise, Paradise will appear before him, and he will see the blessings therein, and he will remain silent for as long as Allah wills. Then he will say, ""O my Lord! Admit me into Paradise."" The Lord will say, ""Did you not say that you would not ask Me for anything else? O son of Adam, how treacherous you are!"" He will say, ""O my Lord! Do not make me the most wretched of Your creation."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: He will keep supplicating until the Lord laughs. When the Lord laughs at him, He will permit him to enter Paradise. When he enters Paradise, it will be said to him, ""Wish for whatever you desire."" He will wish until all his wishes are fulfilled. The Lord will say, ""You will have all this and as much again."" Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say, ""You will have all this and ten times as much."" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I remember these words: You will have all this and as much again."" This is the person who will be the last to enter Paradise."
"7430","I may take shelter in its shade and drink from its water.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The Lord will say, “O son of Adam! If I grant you this, you will ask Me for something else.” He will say, “No, my Lord,” and he will make a covenant that he will not ask for anything else, although the Lord knows that he will do so, for he will not be able to be patient over it. The Lord will bring him near to that tree. He will take shelter in its shade and drink from its water. Then another tree will appear before him, better than the first one, so he will say, “O my Lord, bring me near to it so that I may take shelter in its shade and drink from its water.” The Lord will say, “Did you not make a covenant with Me that you would not ask Me for anything else?” He will say, “Yes, my Lord, but bring me near to it so that I may take shelter in its shade and drink from its water,” and he will make a covenant with the Lord that he will not ask for anything else besides that. The Lord will bring him near to it, although the Lord knows that he will ask for more, for the Lord knows that he will not be able to be patient over it. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then another tree will appear before him near the gate of Paradise, more beautiful than the previous two trees. He will say, “O my Lord, bring me near to this tree so that I may take shelter in its shade and drink from its water.” The Lord will say, “Did you not make a covenant with Me that you would not ask Me for anything else besides this?” He will say, “Yes, my Lord, but bring me near to it.” When he is brought near to it, he will hear the voices of the people of Paradise, so he will say, “O Lord, admit me into Paradise.” Allah, the Exalted, will say, “O son of Adam, will it please you if I give you the world and as much again with it?” He will say, “O my Lord, are You mocking me while You are the Lord of all the worlds?” The Lord will say, “I am not mocking you, but I am able to do whatever I will.” The narrator says: Whenever Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) would mention these words, “Are You mocking me,” he would smile, then he would say: “Will you not ask me why I smiled?” He was asked: “Why did you smile?” He replied: “When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would mention this, he would smile.”"
"7431","""I know the last of the people of the Fire to depart from it. A man will exit it crawling, and he will say: 'O Lord! The people have taken all the places.'"" He said: ""So it will be said to him: 'Go to Paradise to enter Paradise.' So he will go to enter, but he will see that the people have taken all the places. He will return and say: 'O Lord! The people have taken all of the places.' So it will be said to him: 'Do you remember the times you used to live in?' And he will say: 'Yes.' So it will be said to him: 'Wish, He will wish for something, and it will be said to him: 'For you is whatever you wished for, and ten times the world.' He will say: 'Do you mock me while you are the King?'"" He (Ibn Masud) said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laugh until his molars were visible."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2595)"
"7432","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah has entered these people into Hell along with the polytheists, the polytheists will say: Did you not used to say in the world that you are friends? Then why are you with us in Hell? When Allah hears this, He will permit intercession, so the angels and the prophets will intercede for these people until, by Allah's command, they will come out (of Hell). When they are taken out, those people (the disbelievers) will say: Oh, would that we were like them, and intercession would be granted to us, and we too would come out of Hell. So this is the meaning of Allah's statement: ""Soon those who disbelieved will wish that they had been Muslims."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The name of these people in Paradise will be ""Jahannami"" (Hell-dwellers) because their faces will have become blackened. They will say: O our Lord, remove this name from us. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then the Lord will command them to bathe in a river of Paradise, and their (blackness) will be removed."
"7433","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Some people will remain in Hell for as long as Allah wills, then Allah will have mercy on them and bring them out of Hell. They will come to a river at the lowest part of Paradise, whose name will be Haywan. If all the people of the world were to become their guests, they would feed them, give them drink, and present them with gifts (and still the blessings they possess would not be exhausted).”"
"7434","narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the people of faith will be saved from Hell, they will be stopped on a mound between Paradise and Hell, and the wrongs that occurred between them in the world will be requited among them, until when they are purified and cleansed, they will be permitted to enter Paradise. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the person entering Paradise will be more familiar with his specific place than he was with his house in the world."
"7435","The people of Paradise will eat and drink, but they will neither urinate nor defecate, nor will they bring forth phlegm, nor spit. Praise and glorification will be inspired in them just as breathing is inspired, and their food will be eliminated in the form of a burp, whose fragrance will be like that of musk."
"7436","These are some of the ahidith which Abu Huraira reported from Messenger of Allah ﷺ and one is this that he is reported to have said: The (members of the) first group that would be admitted to Paradise would have their faces as bright as full moon during the night. They would neither spit nor suffer catarrh, nor void excrement. They would have their utensils and their combs made of gold and silver and the fuel of their braziers would be aloes and their sweat would be musk and every one of them would have two spouses (so beautiful) that the marrow of their shanks would be visible through the flesh. There would be no dissension amongst them and no enmity in their hearts. Their hearts would be like one heart, glorifying Allah morning and evening. (Using translation from Muslim 2834e)"
"7437","“The first group to enter Paradise will enter with (faces) like the moon in the night when it is full. Then those who follow them will be shining with a light brighter than the brightest star in the sky. They will not urinate or defecate, or blow their noses or spit. Their combs will be of gold, their sweat will be musk, their braziers (receptacle for holding live coals for burning incense) will be pearls and their wives will be houris. Their form will be that of a single man, the form of their father Adam, sixty forearm’s length tall.’” Another chain reports the same. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4333)"
"7438","“I supplicate Allah to bring you and I together in the marketplace of Paradise,” Sa’eed said: “Is there a marketplace there?” He said: “Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ told me that when the people of Paradise enter it, they will take their places according to their deeds, and they will be given permission for a length of time equivalent to Friday on earth, when they will visit Allah. His Throne will be shown to them and He will appear to them in one of the gardens of Paradise. Chairs of light and chairs of pearls and chairs of rubies and chairs of chrysolite and chairs of gold and chairs of silver will be placed for them. Those who are of a lower status than them, and none of them will be regarded as insignificant, will sit on sandhills of musk and camphor, and they will not feel that those who are sitting on chairs are seated better than them.” Abu Hurairah said: “I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord?’ He said: ‘Yes. Do you dispute that you see the sun and the moon on the night when it is full?’ We said: ‘No.’ He said: ‘Likewise, you will not dispute that you see your Lord, the Glorified. There will be no one left in that gathering with whom Allah does not speak face to face, until He will say to a man among you: “Do you not remember, O so-and-so, the day you did such and such?” And He will remind him of some of his sins in this world. He will say: “O Lord, have You not forgiven me?” He will say: “Yes, it is by the vastness of My forgiveness that You have reached the position you are in.” While they are like that, a cloud will cover them from above and will rain down on them perfume the like of whose fragrance they have never smelled before. Then He will say: “Get up and go to the honor that has been prepared for you, and take whatever you desire.” So we will go to a marketplace surrounded by the angels, in which there will be such things as eyes have never seen, ears have never heard and it has not entered the heart of man. Whatever we desire will be carried for us. Nothing will be bought or sold therein. In that marketplace the people of Paradise will meet one another. A man of elevated status will meet those who are of lower status than him, but none shall be regarded as insignificant, and he will be dazzled by the clothes that he sees on him. He will not finish the last of his conversation before better clothes appear on him. That is because no one should be sad there.’” “He said: ‘Then we will go back to our homes where we will be met by our wives, and they will say: ‘Welcome. You have come looking more handsome and with a better fragrance than when you left us.’ And we will say: ‘Today we sat with our Lord, the Compeller, the Glorified, and we deserve to come back as we have come back.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4336)"
"7439","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""When the people of Paradise will enter Paradise, Allah Almighty will say: 'Do you desire anything more so that I may grant you more?' They will say, 'O our Lord! What could be above what You have already given us?' The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then the Lord will say: 'Yes! My pleasure is superior to everything.'\"""""""
"7440","O, Dwellers of Paradise, and they would say in response: At thy service and pleasure, our Lord, the good is in Thy Hand. He (the Lord) would say: Are you well pleased now? They would say: Why should we not be pleased, O Lord, when Thou hast given us what Thou hast not given to any of Thy creatures? He would, however, say: May I not give you (something) even more excellent than that? And they would say: O Lord, what thing can be more excellent than this? And He would say: I shall cause My pleasure to alight upon you and I shall never be afterwards annoyed with you. (Using translation from Muslim 2829)"
"7441","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse: ""For those who have done good is the best [reward] and even more."" The Proph"
"7442","The Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم looked at the full moon on the night of the fourteenth and"
"7443","We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a full moon night. He looked at the moon and said, ""You will certainly see your Lord as you see this moon, and there will be no trouble in seeing Him. So if you can avoid missing (through sleep, business, etc.) a prayer before the rising of the sun (Fajr) and before its setting (ʿAsr) you must do so. He (the Prophet ﷺ ) then recited the following verse: And celebrate the praises Of Your Lord before The rising of the sun And before (its) setting."" (50.39) (Using translation from Bukhārī 573)"
"7444","Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us on the night of the full moon and said, ""You will see your Lord on the Day of Resurrection as you see this (full moon) and you will have no difficulty in seeing Him."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 7436)"
"7445","I not create you? Did I not grant you the ability to see and hear? Did I not get you married? Did I not honor you? Did I not subjugate horses and camels for you? Did I not make you wealthy?"" He will reply, ""Yes, O my Lord!"" The Lord will say, ""Did you ever think that you would meet Me?"" He will reply, ""No, O my Lord."" The Lord will say, ""Today I will forget you just as you forgot Me."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then another person will be presented before his Lord. The Lord will say, ""O so-and-so, did I not create you? Did I not grant you hearing and sight? Did I not get you married? Did I not honor you? Did I not subjugate horses and camels for you? Did I not make you wealthy?"" He will reply, ""Yes, O my Lord."" The Lord will say, ""What preparation did you make for Me?"" He will reply, ""I believed in You, in Your Book, and in Your Messenger. I glorified You, I performed prayer, I fasted."" The Lord will say, ""Well then, shall We not bring witnesses against you?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: That servant will think in his heart, ""Who can bear witness against me?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This is the hypocrite upon whom Allah will be angry. Therefore, Allah will excuse him and a seal will be set upon his mouth, and it will be said to his thighs, ""Speak!"" So his thighs, his bones, his muscles will speak about what he used to do. Then a caller will announce: ""Beware! Every nation should follow that which it used to worship."" So the worshippers of the cross will follow the cross, the worshippers of fire will follow the fire, the worshippers of idols will follow the idols, the worshippers of Satan will follow Satan. Every worshipper of a tyrant will follow the tyrant towards Hell. O people of faith, then we will remain, we who are believers. Our Lord will come to us. We will be standing, and He will say, ""Why are you standing here?"" We will reply, ""We are the believing servants of Allah. We believed in Him, we did not associate anyone with Him. We will remain standing here until our Lord comes. He is our Lord, He will keep us firm."" Then the Lord will say, ""Do you recognize Him?"" We will say, ""Glory be to Him! When He introduces Himself to us, we will recognize Him."" The narrator named Sufyan says: There is a word here which I will not mention before you. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then we will proceed until we come to the Bridge (Sirat) over which there will be hooks made of fire, snatching people. At that place, intercession will be permitted (and it will be said): ""O Allah! Grant safety, grant safety. O Allah, grant safety, grant safety. O Allah, grant safety, grant safety."" When we cross the bridge, then every person who spent a pair of anything from his wealth in the way of Allah, all the gatekeepers of Paradise will call him and say, ""O servant of Allah, O Muslim, this is better. Come here! O servant of Allah, O Muslim, come here, this is better. O servant of Allah, O Muslim, come here, this is better."" Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said—he was present with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) at that time—""Such a person will not suffer any harm; he will enter from one gate or another."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) placed his hand on his shoulder and said, ""I hope that you will be one of them."
"7446","The guardianship of the children of the believers in Paradise will be undertaken by Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him)."
"7447","The Hell and the Paradise fell into dispute and the Hell said: I have been dis- tinguished by the proud and the haughty. And the Paradise said: What is the matter with me that the meek and the humble amongst people and the downtrodden and the simple enter me? Thereupon Allah said to the Paradise: You are (the means) of My Mercy whereby I show mercy to those of My servants whom 1 wish, and He said to the Hell: You are (the means) of punishment whereby 1 punish those of My servants whoml wish. Both of you will be full. The Hell will riot be filled up until Allah puts down His foot in it. The Hell would say: Enough, enough, enough, and at that time it will be filled up, all its parts integrated together. (Using translation from Muslim 2846b)"
"7448","There would be left some space in Paradise as Allah would like that to be left. Then Allah would create another creation as He would like. (Using translation from Muslim 2848d)"
"7449","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of Hell enter Hell, a caller will announce: O people of Paradise, you will remain in it forever, death will not come to you. O people of Hell, you will remain in it forever, death will not come to you.\"""""""
"7450","‘Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and made to stand on the Sirat (the Bridge over Hell). It will be said: “O people of Paradise!” And they will look. Anxious and afraid lest they be brought out of the place they are in. Then it will be said: “O people of Hell!” and they will look, hoping that they will be brought out of the place they are in. Then it will be said: “Do you know what this is?” They will say: “Yes, this is Death.” Then the command will be given for it to be slaughtered on the Sirat, and it will be said to both groups: “It is eternal wherever you are, and there will never be any death therein.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4327)"
"7451","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""None will enter Paradise but will be shown the place he would have occupied in the (Hell) Fire if he had rejected faith, so that he may be more thankful; and none will enter the (Hell) Fire but will be shown the place he would have occupied in Paradise if he had faith, so that may be a cause of sorrow for him."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6569)"
"7452","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""None of the people of Paradise will wish to return to the world, even if he were to be given ten times the world and all that is in it. Only the martyr is different, for he will wish to return to the world and be killed ten times because of the virtue (he sees) in martyrdom.\"""""""
"7453","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The people of Paradise will be of three types. A ruler who is just and has been granted success, a person who is merciful and soft-hearted, who does good to every relative and Muslim, and a person who is poor, avoids begging, and gives charity and alms."
"7454","I will punish through you whomever I wish.' And He said to Paradise: 'You are My mercy; you encompass everything.' Nevertheless, both of you will be filled."
"7455","""I looked into Paradise and I saw that the most of its people were the poor; and I looked into the Fire and I saw that most of its people were women."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2602)"
"7456","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saw both Paradise and Hell with his blessed body and with his eyes; this was a favor from Allah Almighty upon him so that, through this, a distinction would be made between him and the other prophets. As for the attributes which you described, that you saw the inhabitants of Paradise characterized with those attributes and the inhabitants of Hell characterized with those attributes, these are the attributes whose forms were presented before you so that, through them, you may know the objectives of the ends of means for your Ummah in both worlds, so that you may encourage your Ummah through the information of these attributes so that they may seek them, and warn them through the attributes of Hell so that they may avoid adopting those characteristics which can lead to Hell."
"7457","Amongst the inmates of Paradise the women would form a minority. (Using translation from Muslim 2738a)"
"7458","I hope that you will be half of the people of Paradise, and only a Muslim will enter Paradise. On the Day of Resurrection, in comparison to the disbelievers, the number of Muslims will be like a white hair on the body of a black ox, or a black hair on the body of a white ox."
"7459","""The people of Paradise are a hundred and twenty rows, eighty of them are from this nation, and forty are from the rest of the nations."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2546)"
"7460","""The people of Paradise are a hundred and twenty rows, eighty of them are from this nation, and forty are from the rest of the nations."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2546)"
"7461","Two are the types of the denizens of Hell whom I did not see: people having flogs like the tails of the ox with them and they would be beating people, and the women who would be dressed but appear to be naked, who would be inclined (to evil) and make their husbands incline towards it. Their heads would be like the humps of the bukht camel inclined to one side. They will not enter Paradise and they would not smell its odour whereas its odour would be smelt from such and such distance. (Using translation from Muslim 2128)"
"7462","The fire which sons of Adam burn is only one-seventieth part of the Fire of Hell. His Companions said: By Allah, even ordinary fire would have been enough (to burn people). Thereupon he said: It is sixty-nine parts in excess of (the heat of) fire in this world each of them being equivalent to their heat. (Using translation from Muslim 2843a)"
"7463","narrates: He learned of this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Your fire is one seventieth part of the fire of Hell. Sea water has been poured over it. If it were not so, Allah would not have placed any benefit in it for anyone."
"7464","Sayyiduna Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him): He stood on the eastern wall of Bayt al-Maqdis and began to weep. Someone as"
"7465","Sayyiduna Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) stood on the eastern wall of Bayt al-Maqdis and began to weep. When he was asked about it, he said: Regarding this place, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) informed that from here he saw Malik, the (keeper) of Hell, turning over embers as if they were grape seeds."
"7466","“The Fire complained to its Lord and said: ‘O Lord, parts of me have consumed other parts.’ So He gave it two occasions to exhale, one in winter and one in summer. The intense cold that you feel (in winter) is part of its severe frost (Zamharir) and the intense heat that you feel in summer is part of its hot wind (Samum).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4319)"
"7467","that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""Woe is the valley of Jahannam, the disbeliever shall drop into it for forty autumns before he reaches its bottom."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3164)"
"7468","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If a stone is thrown into Hell, it will keep falling for seventy years before it reaches its bottom."
"7469","We were in the company of Messenger of Allah ﷺ that we heard a terrible sound. Thereupon Allah's Apostle ﷺ said: Do you know what (sound) is this? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. Thereupon he said: That is a stone which was thrown seventy years before in Hell and it has'been constantly slipping down and now it has reached its base. (Using translation from Muslim 2844a)"
"7470","“O you who believe! Have fear of Allah as is His due, and die not except as Muslims. [3:102] (Then he said): ‘If a drop of Zaqqum were to be dropped on the earth, it would ruin the livelihood of the people of this world, so how about those who have no food other than it (i.e. Zaqqum)?’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4325)"
"7471","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There will be some snakes in Hell which will be like the necks of Bactrian camels. If any one of them bites, its pain will be felt for forty years."
"7472","The lightest punishment in Hell will be for the person who will be made to wear shoes of fire, and because of them his brain will be boiling."
"7473","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""There will be water like tar."" This refers to tar. When he approaches it, as a result, the skin of his face will peel off."
"7474","When the inmates of Paradise would go to Paradise and the inmates of Hell would go to Hell, death would be called and it would be placed between the Paradise and the Hell and then slaughtered and then the announcer would announce: O inmates of Paradise, no death. O inmates of Hell-Fire, no death. And it would increase the delight of the inmates of Paradise and it would increase the grief of the inmates of Hell-Fire. (Using translation from Muslim 2850b)"
"7475","“I know the last of the people of Hell who will be brought forth from it, and the last of the people of Paradise to be admitted to Paradise. (It is) a man who will emerge from Hell crawling, and it will be said to him: ‘Go and enter Paradise.’ He will come to it and it will be made to appear to him as if it is full.’ Allah will say: ‘Go and enter Paradise.’ He will come to it and it will appear to him as if it is full. So he will say: ‘O Lord, I found it full.’ Allah will say: ‘Go and enter Paradise.’ He will come to it and it will be made to appear to him as if it is full. So he will say: ‘O Lord, I found it full.’ Allah will say: ‘Go and enter Paradise, for you will have the like of the world and ten times more, or you will have ten times the like of the world.’ He will say: ‘Are You mocking me, or are You laughing at me, when You are the Sovereign?’” He said: ""And I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiling so broadly that his molar teeth could be seen."" And he used to say: ""This is the lowest of the people of Paradise in status."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4339)"
"7476","I will punish whom I will.' And He said to Paradise: 'You are My mercy; through you I will show mercy to whom I will.' And each of you will be filled."
"7477","I will have mercy on whom I wish. And He said to Hell: You are My punishment; through you I will punish whom I wish. And both of you will be filled."
"7478","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded women to give charity and encouraged them to do so. He said: ""Give charity, f"
"7479","Sayyiduna Hakim bin Hizam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: One day, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) addressed the women, giving them advice and admonition, and commanded them to fear Allah and obey their husbands. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Some women among you will enter Paradise—the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) brought his fingers together—and some women will be the fuel of Hell—the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) spread his fingers apart while saying this. Then one of the women, who belonged to the Maard or perhaps Murad tribe, asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is the reason for this? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Because you are ungrateful to your husbands, you curse excessively, and you avoid doing good."
"7480","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The woman who buries alive and the one who is buried alive will be in Hell."" The same narration, with another chain, is also reported from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) These words of the narration are regarding the women of the disbelievers, not about the Muslims. The statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""The woman who buries alive and the one who is buried alive"" refers to those women who are associated with the disbelievers. They will be in Hell."
"7481","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three types of people were presented before me who will enter Hell first: (one) a ruler who imposes himself, (second) a wealthy person who does not fulfill Allah's right, (third) a poor person who is arrogant."
"7482","Sayyiduna Iyad bin Himar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""The people of Hell are of five types: the weak person who is not cared about and who lives among you as a follower (obedient to others); he neither desires wife and children, nor wealth.\"" (The narrator says) I asked: O Abu Abdullah! Will there be such people? He replied: Yes, by Allah! I found such people in the time of ignorance, who used to guard the tribe only so"
"7483","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrates: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saying this: I heard it with these two ears. He pointed towards both his ears and said this: (The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said:) \""Allah Almighty will take some people out of Hell and admit them into Paradise.\"" In Amr's narration, these are the words. A person said to him: Allah Almighty has said: \""Those people will intend to come out"
"7484","I met Shu’bah. I narrated this hadith to him, so Shu’bah informed me that Qatadah narrated this from Sayyiduna Anas. However, Shu’bah used the word 'dharr' instead of 'al-dharr.' Yazid states: In this narration, the narrator named Abu Bastam has fabricated. Yazid says: I met Imran Qattan. I narrated this hadith to him, so Imran informed me: Qatadah narrated this hadith to me from Ata bin Yazid Laithi, from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). Yazid says: In this narration, Imran made a mistake and was confused in it."
"7485","narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""As for the people of Hell who are its rightful inhabitants, they will neither die in it nor will they live. However, there will be some people whom the Fire will reach due to their sins, and it will kill them, until they become like charcoal, then intercession will be made for them."
"7486","The thickness of the disbeliever will be forty-two cubits, according to the cubit of the Jabbar, and his height will be like the mountain of Uhud."" Jabbar was the ruler of Yemen and was called Jabbar."
"7487","The molar tooth of an unbeliever or the canine teeth of an unbeliever will be like Uhud and the thickness of his skin a three night's journey. (Using translation from Muslim 2851)"
"7488","The molar tooth of a disbeliever will be like the Uhud mountain (the narrator says: that is, it will be so in Hell)."
"7489","The cat would scratch her from the front and from the back. I saw in Hell a man from the tribe of Banu Dadda’ who used to steal the belongings of pilgrims with his stick; when he was caught, he would say, 'This thing got stuck to my stick.' And I saw the man who had stolen two sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah."
"7490","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You are a Muslim and he is a disbeliever."
"7491","The angels replied: This is Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him), Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him), and Sayyiduna Isa (peace be upon him). These gentlemen are waiting for you."
